course: dictionary
lesson: 871
title: Billiard, the word that describes things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Billiard is a word that often sits in front of another word to describe it, like a billiard table or a billiard ball. When it does this, it tells you which kind of table or ball you mean. Billiards, with an s, is the name of the game itself.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Then, one very dark, wet, windy night, the Wild Wooders attacked... stoats into the conservatory and billiard-room.» A conservatory is a glass room, and a billiard-room is another room in a big house. The word room tells you what kind of room it is: a room with a billiard table in it.
explain: Notice the word that comes after billiard. In «billiard table» and «billiard ball», the word after tells you what the thing is, and billiard tells you what it belongs to. Ask yourself: is this word describing something, or naming the game?
fact: Billiard is an adjective when it sits before a noun, as in «billiard table», «billiard room» and «billiard ball».
fact: Billiards, with an s, is a noun for the game itself, and it is uncountable: you do not say one billiards.
fact: Billiards is played on a large table covered in green cloth, where players hit balls with a long stick called a cue.
fact: Snooker and pool are related games, so they are close cousins of billiards.
fact: In «bald as a billiard ball», the phrase means completely bald, with a smooth, round head like a ball.

exercise: «Stoats held the conservatory, the billiard-room and the French windows.» What kind of room is the billiard-room? | A room where food is cooked | A room for reading books | A room full of glass plants | *A room for playing billiards, with a large green table
exercise: Billiards is a game. What do players hit the balls with? | Their hands only | A bat, like in cricket | A racket, like in tennis | *A long stick called a cue
exercise: In the phrase «billiard ball», which word tells you what kind of ball it is? | ball | bald | *billiard | table
test: Billiards, snooker and pool are... | Different sports played on grass | *Related games | Kinds of cloth | Names for the same bat
test: When a billiard ball hits the cushion, the angle it bounces off is... | *Equal to the angle it hit the cushion at | Bigger than the angle it hit at | Zero, so the ball stops | Always a right angle
exam: Which phrase uses billiard to describe a noun? | *a billiard table in the hall | the billiards was fun all afternoon | billiards is a game | played billiard on the lawn
